<h3>About Identity Verification for Refunds</h3>
<p>To process a €14,280 refund to a new bank account, we require identity verification:</p>
<ol>
<li><b>Government-issued photo ID</b> — passport or national ID of the account holder</li>
<li><b>Proof of bank account ownership</b> — bank statement showing the account number</li>
<li><b>Company authorization</b> — if the refund is to a corporate account, a letter from your finance department</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFEBEE;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we can't refund to the new AMEX card automatically:</b> Corporate card reissuance creates a new card number that isn't linked to the original transaction in our system. While we could refund to your Airbnb account credit, this wouldn't work for corporate accounting (your finance team needs the funds returned to a bank account for reconciliation). Bank transfer is the only option for corporate refunds when the original card has been reissued. The €14,280 will arrive in your account within 3-5 business days after verification.
</p>

<p><b>Option 2 — Airbnb Credit (instant):</b></p>
<p>Receive €14,280 as Airbnb travel credit. However, this cannot be used for corporate expense reconciliation and may not be acceptable to your finance department.</p>

